{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Until the death of the high priest.</b> It has already been explained that the exile falls upon the unintentional manslayer. And since the categories of unintentional acts are not equal — some being close to compulsion and some close to deliberate intent — He assigned an unequal duration of exile for all the unintentional slayers: for some, their error occurs shortly before the death of the priest; for others, the slayer dies in exile before the priest dies. This is by the just judgment of the blessed El, who knows and so punishes the unintentional manslayer according to the degree of his error, as it says: וְהָאֱלֹהִים אִנָּה לְיָדוֹ (Exodus 21:13)."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:41:41.620252006Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}